BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (Use a small evidence architecture with explicit lineage. SQLite is sufficient for an initial desk if one controlled writer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (handles imports; PostgreSQL becomes useful when concurrent work and access separation justify the operational) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (burden. Store entities, assets, source observations, ownership assertions, contracts, reporting periods, and exceptions as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (separate tables. An ownership assertion must reference evidence, scope, and effective dates; it must not overwrite the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (raw registry observation. Keep original PDFs, CSVs, and JSON responses in versioned object storage with access) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (controls and retention aligned to source permissions. Calculate SHA-256 digests using Python's hashlib, but remember) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (that a digest detects later changes rather than proving that the original claim was true. Use deterministic record keys) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (and ingestion identifiers so rerunning a job does not duplicate licenses or obligations. Separate retrieved_at,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (source_updated_at, effective_from, and effective_to timestamps. Preserve currency, units, timezone, and source) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (precision rather than normalizing them away without a trace. Every dashboard assertion should resolve to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (underlying observation and document. This structure makes a rights dispute or royalty challenge answerable through) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (evidence, instead of requiring the operator to reconstruct months of decisions from email threads. Keep correction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (history append-only where source permissions allow.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (Build connectors as short, testable adapters. Python's urllib.request, csv, json, sqlite3, decimal, and unittest can support) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (a lean first implementation without third-party dependencies. Configure credentials outside source files, redact them) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (from logs, and separate read access from administrative permissions. A connector should emit a source identifier,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (retrieval timestamp, response digest, schema version, and explicit success or failure state. Validate required fields) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (before loading transformed tables. A provider returning an HTML login page with a successful HTTP status must fail) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (content validation rather than enter the warehouse as usable data. Handle pagination with saved checkpoints and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (deduplicate on stable identifiers. Use conditional requests where supported, bounded retries for transient failures, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (immediate escalation for revoked credentials. Diagnose HTTP behavior with curl or Postman against authorized) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (endpoints, inspect certificates with OpenSSL, and use SQL EXPLAIN when queries slow down. For document) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (comparisons, use difflib on extracted text and retain the original page reference. OCR output is a search aid, not the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (governing contract text. A single misread decimal or omitted exception can reverse an obligation, so verify extracted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (rates and deadlines against the signed document before activating calculations or alerts.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (Define refresh cadence by decision risk rather than by the availability of a scheduler. Recheck title and status before an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (offer, signature, renewal, or material expansion of territory; monitor active assets at a cadence matched to the relevant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 191.35 Tm (source and contract. Refresh royalty reporting when a statement arrives, then reconcile it against the agreed delivery) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.12 Tm (deadline. Store renewal, notice, cure, audit, and minimum-guarantee dates as structured obligations with named owners) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 160.90 Tm (and separate reminder offsets. Calendar reminders alone cannot distinguish an expiring license from an auto-renewal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 145.67 Tm (requiring timely cancellation. The engineering contractor runs daily connector health checks, while the operator) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 130.45 Tm (reviews only changes that alter a decision or require action. Test against frozen sample records: renamed owners, split) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.22 Tm (territories, duplicate statement uploads, missing pages, refunded sales, and expired API keys. Track source age, parse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.00 Tm (failures, unmatched identifiers, and unresolved obligations on one exception board. Require each exception to carry an) Tj ET
